1
00:04:28,571 --> 00:04:34,571
Saints and Soldiers: Airborne Creed is a war, drama,
action film directed by Ryan Little.

2
00:08:57,142 --> 00:09:03,142
On August 15, 1944 the 517th Parachute Regimental Combat
Team (PRCT) jumped over the south of France.

3
00:13:25,714 --> 00:13:31,714
Their mission was to support and protect the Allied Troops marching to Berlin.

4
00:17:54,285 --> 00:18:00,285
Landing in enemy territory, they fell under immediate attack.

5
00:22:22,857 --> 00:22:28,857
In their effort to complete the mission and rendez-vous with their unit, three isolated
paratroopers come across a group of French resistants in desperate need.

6
00:26:51,428 --> 00:26:57,428
They decide to help liberate some of the captive Partisans.

7
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Doing so they will risk their lives.

8
00:35:48,571 --> 00:35:54,571
Corporal James Rossi, played by Corbin Allred.

9
00:40:17,142 --> 00:40:23,142
Sergeant Caleb Jones, played by David Nibley.

10
00:44:45,714 --> 00:44:51,714
Corporal Harland 'Bud' Curtis, played by Jasen Wade.

11
00:49:14,285 --> 00:49:20,285
Emilie, played by Virginie Fourtina Anderson.

12
00:53:42,857 --> 00:53:48,857
Erich Neumann, played by Lincoln Hoppe.

13
00:58:11,428 --> 00:58:17,428
Charlotte, played by Nichelle Aiden.

14
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
Saints and Soldiers: Airborne Creed is a 2012 war drama film directed
by Ryan Little and produced by Little and Adam Abel.

15
01:07:08,571 --> 01:07:14,571
It is the second installment in the Saints and Soldiers film series, and is based on
events that took place during the invasion of Southern France in World War II.

16
01:11:37,142 --> 01:11:43,142
The film stars Corbin Allred, David Nibley, and Jasen Wade.

17
01:16:05,714 --> 01:16:11,714
The film was shot in Utah, on a tight budget, saving money by using
volunteer World War II reenactors as some of the actors and extras.

18
01:20:34,285 --> 01:20:40,285
The film received mixed reviews; many critics found the film mediocre,
yet still praised the performances and cinematography.

19
01:25:02,857 --> 01:25:08,857
The film explores themes of world war ii, us army, family
relationships, u.s. soldier, mormon missionary.

20
01:29:31,428 --> 01:29:37,428
The tone is emotional.
